<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George V of Hanover</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1819">1819</a>–<a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hanover">House of Hanover</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George V of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> was the last king of Hanover, reigning from 1851 to 1866. Blind from youth, he ruled conservatively and sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866. His army won at Langensalza but surrendered two days later, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> annexed the kingdom. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-v-of-hanover.jpg" alt="George V of Hanover" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_George_V_of_Hannover_10.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>George was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> on 27 May 1819, the only legitimate son of Prince Ernest Augustus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-king-of-hanover">Duke of Cumberland</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a>, and Princess Frederica of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>. He spent his childhood in Berlin and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>. He lost the sight of one eye after an illness in 1828 and of the other after an accident in 1833.</p><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> succeeded to the British throne in 1837, the personal union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> ended because Hanover's semi-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salic-law">Salic law</a> barred a woman, and George became Crown Prince of Hanover. Because he was totally blind there were doubts about his fitness, but his father decided that he should succeed. He married Princess Marie of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a> on 18 February 1843.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>George succeeded his father on 18 November 1851. From his father and his uncle Duke Charles of Mecklenburg he had learned a high and autocratic view of royal authority, and during his fifteen years as king he often quarrelled with the Hanoverian Landtag. Unlike his father he disliked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, which bordered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> on the west and east, and he generally supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the Diet of the German Confederation. He supported industry: in 1856 a company named after him and his wife founded an iron and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> works that gave the city Georgsmarienhütte its name.</p><p>In June 1866 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> demanded an alliance and the submission of Hanoverian troops. Against the wishes of his parliament George refused and joined the Austrian side. The Hanoverian army of 20,600 men, though tactically successful at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-langensalza-1866">Battle of Langensalza</a>, was hopelessly outnumbered and surrendered on 29 June 1866. Prussia annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> on 20 September 1866. George rejected an abdication in favour of his son proposed by Queen Marie.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>George went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and never renounced his rights or accepted the annexation. From 1866 to 1870 he maintained the Guelphic Legion, partly at his own expense, hoping a Franco-Prussian war would restore his kingdom. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> then confiscated his private assets, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a> had managed as the Guelph Fund against Guelph activities. He was made honorary general in the British Army in 1876 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 12 June 1878. He was buried in St George's Chapel at Windsor Castle.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “George V of Hanover” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>George V</b>, blind from youth, became king in 1851.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-hanover">Kingdom of Hanover</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=52.52,13.38&amp;year=1857" aria-label="Berlin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of George V of Hanover"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5690 5568h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5690 5568h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=52.52,13.38&amp;year=1857">What was here in 1857? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
